Phase OS-10: Kernel TCP/IP Networking Stack - 3 new kernel ASM modules:

1. kernel/net_ip.asm (IPv4/IPv6 Packet Processing)
   - AArch64 ASM implementation of IP layer packet handling
   - IPv4: header parse/build, checksum, fragmentation/reassembly, routing table lookup
   - IPv6: header parse, extension headers, flow label processing
   - ARP: address resolution cache (64 entries), request/reply handling
   - ICMP: echo request/reply (ping), destination unreachable, TTL exceeded
   - Route table: 128 entries with metric, gateway, interface binding
   - Export symbols: net_ip_init, net_ip_send, net_ip_recv, net_ip_route_add, net_ip_arp_resolve
   - Integration: called from net.asm and net_tls.asm for IP layer services

2. kernel/net_tcp.asm (TCP Connection Management)
   - AArch64 ASM implementation of TCP protocol
   - Connection states: CLOSED/SYN_SENT/SYN_RCVD/ESTABLISHED/FIN_WAIT/CLOSE_WAIT/LAST_ACK/TIME_WAIT
   - Three-way handshake: SYN, SYN-ACK, ACK processing
   - Flow control: sliding window (64KB), congestion window (slow start, AIMD)
   - Retransmission: RTO calculation (Jacobson algorithm), timeout queue (32 slots)
   - Segment processing: sequence numbers, acknowledgment, checksum verification
   - Max 64 simultaneous connections, 2048 segment reassembly buffer
   - Export symbols: net_tcp_init, net_tcp_connect, net_tcp_listen, net_tcp_send, net_tcp_recv, net_tcp_close
   - Integration: called from net_tls.asm for TCP transport

3. kernel/net_udp.asm (UDP Datagram Service)
   - AArch64 ASM implementation of UDP protocol
   - Connectionless datagram send/receive
   - Port binding: 128 port slots, multicast group support (16 groups)
   - Checksum computation and verification (with IP pseudo-header)
   - Receive queue: 256 datagrams max, per-port queue (32 each)
   - DNS integration: port 53 default handler for net_dns.asm calls
   - Broadcast/multicast: 255.255.255.255 broadcast, IGMP-lite group join
   - Export symbols: net_udp_init, net_udp_bind, net_udp_send, net_udp_recv, net_udp_join_multicast
   - Integration: called by DNS resolver, DHCP client, NTP client

All modules follow existing kernel conventions (.arch armv8-a, .global exports, stp/ldp frame setup).
